{%- comment -%}
  Usage: class="sec {% render 'surface-class', s: section.settings.surface %}"

  chalk is the page default and needs no class. jute is the warm alternate that
  most sections swap to. mist is the cool one, and it exists for a different
  job: chalk and jute are both warm neutrals, so alternating them reads as
  texture rather than structure, and a reader scrolling a long single-product
  page gets no signal about where storytelling ends and shopping begins.

  mist is deliberately offered on fewer sections than the other two. Its whole
  value is being the one temperature change on the page — put it on four
  sections and it stops marking anything.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if s == 'jute' -%}surf-jute{%- elsif s == 'mist' -%}surf-mist{%- endif -%}
